Chapter 2
Portfolios, diversification, beta and the CAPM
المحافظ الاستثمارية والتنويع ومعامل بيتا ونموذج تسعير الأصول الرأسمالية
Chapter 1 ended on a sentence that needs a formula: only systematic risk is rewarded. This chapter supplies it, and in doing so supplies the number that the whole of corporate finance runs on — the required return on a company's equity.
The route has four steps. A portfolio's return is easy and its risk is not, because two assets that move apart offset each other. The offsetting is measured by correlation, and as more assets are added the company-specific part of the risk falls away, leaving only the part that moves with the market. That remaining part, scaled against the market itself, is beta. And a required return built on beta is the Capital Asset Pricing Model.
Figure F602-01 is your map.
Figure F602-01. Chapter 2 roadmap: from two assets to beta to a required return.
