LANGUAGE FOCUS   "Expected"
English expected in finance means the probability-weighted average of the outcomes, not what anybody anticipates in the ordinary sense and not what is likely. An expected return of 8.5 per cent can be an outcome that cannot occur at all, as it was in Chapter 1. Arabic المتوقع carries the everyday sense of anticipation and has to be read technically here. French espéré is the technical term, deliberately distinct from attendu or prévu, and the French usage is the clearer of the three. Note the pairing the exam relies on: expected return against required return, where the first is a forecast and the second is a standard, and reading either as the other reverses the buy-or-sell conclusion.
